{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-97354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2(k\\cdot (-3))+5\\cdot (-3\\cdot 2)+3\\cdot (4\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-6k-30+36 \\\\  & =6-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6-6k & =0 \\\\ 6k & =6 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-97354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-1\\cdot (-2))+4\\cdot (1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-4+8+4k \\\\  & =4+4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4+4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =-4 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-44057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-44057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot (-1\\cdot k)+3\\cdot (2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-2-2k+18 \\\\  & =16-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ 16-2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =16 \\\\ k & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-44057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-44057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-44057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-44057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (2\\cdot (-2))+k\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-3-16+k \\\\  & =k-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ k-19 & =0 \\\\ k & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-97347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-13"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "19"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "19"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot ((-4)\\cdot (-3))+k\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =48+2k+0 \\\\  & =48+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ 48+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-48 \\\\ k & =-24\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-97352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-19"] ["math" "-24"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "27"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-4)y(-4)+x(2)y(2)+x(4)y(4).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=k-2t$ and $q(t)=5-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-4)q(-4)+p(2)q(2)+p(4)q(4) \\\\  & =(k+8)(5-8)+(k-4)(5-2)+(k-8)(5-8) \\\\  & =(-3k-24)+(3k-12)+(-3k+24) \\\\  & =-3k-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3k-12 & =0 \\\\ 3k & =-12 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-97355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{1}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $1,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-1)y(-1)+x(1)y(1).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=2t+4$ and $q(t)=kt+2$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2)(-k+2)+(6)(k+2) \\\\  & =-2k+4+6k+12 \\\\  & =4k+16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4k+16 & =0 \\\\ 4k & =-16 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-140266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=1+{t}^{2}$ and $q(t)=-5{t}^{2}+2t+k$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2)(k-7)+(1)(k)+(2)(k-3) \\\\  & =2k-14+k+2k-6 \\\\  & =5k-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5k-20 & =0 \\\\ 5k & =20 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "28772962f48fd527a4a6fc12b1d4e3eb292fab7e2e3f74e14c0ac6ea8b4a19b3"} {"question" "q-140265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040652/state.json" "file_sha256" "452ffba4b697205c95375627cf63df8f9cb199f1414f7ded71ea68de16b5d976"} {"question" "q-140265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4